@@ -0,0 +1,15 @@
+## Context
+
+`src/domain/` must not read the clock. Task functions in `task.ts` are pure; `list.ts` composes them.
+
+## Decisions
+
+- Pure task functions take the time as a last parameter, `now: string` (an ISO-8601 string): `createTask(input, id, now)`, `completeTask(task, now)`, `reopenTask`, `renameTask`, `addTag`, `removeTag`. Each returns the task with `updatedAt: now`; `createTask` sets both fields.
+- `createTaskList(now: () => string)` takes a clock and calls it once per successful operation, after lookups and validation, so failures never touch a task.
+- `createTodoList(now = () => new Date().toISOString())` in `src/index.ts`, which is outside `src/domain/`, supplies the real clock by default; callers (and tests) may pass their own.
+- Assumption: any successful call of the five operations sets `updatedAt`, even when the content ends up the same (e.g. tagging with a tag already present).
+- `Task` gains `readonly createdAt: string` and `readonly updatedAt: string`, with no new export.
+
+## Risks
+
+Changing the signatures of exported task functions affects callers inside the repo only (`list.ts`, tests); they are not exported from `src/index.ts`.
