@@ -0,0 +1,24 @@
+## Why
+
+The app should show how old a task is and what changed recently. For that, each task must record when it was created and when it was last changed.
+
+## What Changes
+
+- Every task gets `createdAt` and `updatedAt`, ISO-8601 date-time strings.
+- A task just added has the same value in both.
+- Completing, reopening, renaming, tagging or untagging a task sets its `updatedAt` to the time of the change; `createdAt` never changes.
+- The domain does not read the clock: the pure task functions take the time as a parameter, and the list takes a clock function when it is created.
+
+## Capabilities
+
+### New Capabilities
+- `task-timestamps`: creation and last-change times on every task.
+
+### Modified Capabilities
+None.
+
+## Impact
+
+- Project rules touched: "No wall clock or randomness in the domain" (the time is passed in by the caller; the default clock lives in `src/index.ts`, outside `src/domain/`), "TSDoc on every exported function" (updated for changed signatures), "Errors are returned as a Result" (unchanged; failed operations do not change a task). No new dependency.
+- Public API in `src/index.ts`: `createTodoList` gains an optional clock parameter, and the `Task` type gains two fields. No new export.
+- `src/domain/task.ts`, `src/domain/list.ts`, `src/index.ts`, `test/`.
